  organization = {Baltic Road Association},
  note = {http://www.balticroads.org},
  abstract = {Since 1996 the Falling Weight Deflectometer (FWD) is used to characterize
	the bearing capacity of pavement structures in Estonia. The deflection
	data of the load cell, mounted in the center of the loading plate
	of the FWD, is used for calculation of the pavement equivalent E-modulus.
	At the same time FWD has 6 additional load cells, which are mounted
	at different distances from the center of the loading plate and based
	on the FWD deflection measurement data we can create the deflection
	basin characterizing the pavement condition at the FWD test site.
	For further and more complete utilization of the FWD measurement
	data, citerias for the different deflection basin parameters (surface
	curvature index - SCI, base damage index - BDI, base curvature index
	- BDI) were determined. Based on those FWD measurement-based parameters
	- pavement equivalent E-modulus value and deflection basin parameters
	– a system for pavement structural evaluation and repair design was
